# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad — AutoCAD prints (type v) of a VARIANT / SAFEARRAY in lower case
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: a CAD run of probes/sources/probe-type-symbols.lsp on AutoCAD and BricsCAD
#+BRANCH: fix-type-symbols-print-lowercase-on-autocad
#+DATE: 2026-10-08

* Observation

intersectwith-probe.lsp prints =(vl-princ-to-string (type v))=:

| target                         | variant   | its safearray |
|--------------------------------+-----------+---------------|
| AutoCAD 2022 (job 17029587295) | variant   | safearray     |
| BricsCAD V25 / V26             | VARIANT   | SAFEARRAY     |
| clautolisp (any dialect)       | VARIANT   | SAFEARRAY     |

=(eq (type v) 'VARIANT)= is true on AutoCAD all the same (the probe takes
that branch), so the symbol is the same and only its printed name differs.
VLA-OBJECT prints in upper case on AutoCAD too.

* Proposal

Measure which TYPE results AutoCAD prints in lower case (variant,
safearray, maybe others) with vl-princ-to-string, prin1, princ and
vl-symbol-name; if confirmed, print them that way under the AutoCAD
dialects (a divergence to classify per AGENTS.md).

* Status (2026-10-22)

Not implemented: the measured evidence is not enough to decide WHAT to
change. The only AutoCAD datum is one row of intersectwith-probe.lsp
(job 17029587295): =(vl-princ-to-string (type v))= is "variant" /
"safearray". probe-results/autocad/ holds no transcript of that run, and
nothing measures:

- =vl-prin1-to-string= and =vl-symbol-name= of those TYPE results, i.e.
  whether the symbol's NAME is lower case (then =vl-symbol-name=, =strcat=
  of it and =read= round trips all change) or only its printed form;
- whether the literal symbol (='VARIANT=, =(read "VARIANT")=) prints in
  lower case too on AutoCAD, i.e. whether the symbol is interned with a
  lower-case name everywhere, independently of TYPE;
- the other TYPE results (PICKSET, FILE, SUBR, USUBR, EXRXSUBR, INT, REAL,
  STR, SYM, LIST). VLA-OBJECT and ENAME are known upper case on AutoCAD
  (the observation above; block-walk probe, run 20261003T130228Z).

The BricsCAD side is likewise vl-princ-to-string only.

New probe suite: probes/sources/probe-type-symbols.lsp, registered in
probes/sources/manifest.txt (=make probe=, or =PROBE_SUITES=type-symbols=).
For every kind of value it records vl-princ-to-string, vl-prin1-to-string
and vl-symbol-name of =(type v)=, and whether it is EQ to the upper-case
symbol read back; for each type name, how the literal symbol prints (upper
and lower case spellings, quoted in source) and atoms-family of VARIANT /
SAFEARRAY. Checked under clautolisp (--dialect autocad-2022): every row
runs, all upper case.

Next: run it on AutoCAD 2022 and BricsCAD V26, commit the results under
probe-results/, then implement exactly what they show under the AutoCAD
dialects (printer only vs symbol name), with the --strict portability
handling used for comparable divergences and a "*** clautolisp" note on
the TYPE page of the specification.

* Measured (2026-10-23)

probe-type-symbols.lsp on AutoCAD 2022 Windows (run 20261023T074943Z),
BricsCAD V25 Windows (20261023T075150Z), BricsCAD V26 macOS
(20261023T031215Z). Both BricsCAD builds agree on every row.

(type v) of each kind of value:

| value          | AutoCAD vl-symbol-name / princ / prin1 | eq read upcase | BricsCAD V25 / V26 |
|----------------+----------------------------------------+----------------+--------------------|
| variant        | variant                                | T              | VARIANT            |
| variant of SA  | variant                                | T              | VARIANT            |
| safearray      | safearray                              | T              | SAFEARRAY          |
| vla-object     | (type gave nil: no acad object there)  | -              | VLA-OBJECT         |
| ename          | ENAME                                  | T              | ENAME              |
| pickset        | PICKSET                                | T              | PICKSET            |
| file           | FILE                                   | T              | FILE               |
| subr car       | SUBR                                   | T              | SUBR               |
| usubr (defun)  | SUBR                                   | T              | SUBR               |
| exrxsubr       | EXRXSUBR                               | T              | EXRXSUBR           |
| int real str   | INT REAL STR                           | T              | INT REAL STR       |
| sym list       | SYM LIST                               | T              | SYM LIST           |

The literal symbols, independently of TYPE (vl-princ-to-string and
vl-symbol-name of (read "NAME"), vl-princ-to-string of (read "name")):

| literal                      | AutoCAD   | BricsCAD  |
|------------------------------+-----------+-----------|
| VARIANT / variant            | variant   | VARIANT   |
| SAFEARRAY / safearray        | safearray | SAFEARRAY |
| 'VARIANT quoted in source    | variant   | VARIANT   |
| 'safearray quoted in source  | safearray | SAFEARRAY |
| VLA-OBJECT ENAME PICKSET FILE SUBR USUBR EXRXSUBR INT REAL STR SYM LIST | upper | upper |
| (atoms-family 1 '("VARIANT" "SAFEARRAY")) | ("VARIANT" "SAFEARRAY") | same |

Conclusion: on AutoCAD it is the symbol's NAME that is lower case -- for the
two symbols VARIANT and SAFEARRAY only, whatever produced them (TYPE, a
quoted literal, READ of any spelling) -- not a TYPE or printer quirk. The
reader stays case-insensitive: every spelling reads as the same symbol,
(eq (type v) 'VARIANT) and (eq (type v) (read (strcase (vl-symbol-name
(type v))))) are T. (Same mechanism as the mixed-case vl-symbol-name of
'vlax-vbEmpty in the activex-constants inventory: AutoCAD keeps the case
its own code interned a symbol with.) BricsCAD: all upper case.

Implemented (2026-10-23): safe, since identity and reading do not change,
only the name the symbol shows.

- clautolisp/autolisp-runtime/source/api.lisp: AUTOLISP-SYMBOL-PRINT-NAME
  (exported) -- the canonical name, except "variant" / "safearray" for
  VARIANT / SAFEARRAY under every dialect whose product is not BricsCAD
  (*AUTOCAD-LOWER-CASE-SYMBOL-NAMES*); AUTOLISP-VL-SYMBOL-NAME uses it. The
  symbol is still interned under "VARIANT", and every internal name
  comparison (AUTOLISP-SYMBOL-NAME) is unchanged.
- clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp: AUTOLISP-VALUE->STRING
  (princ, prin1, print, vl-princ-to-string, vl-prin1-to-string, the REPL
  echo) prints symbols with it.
- Spec: "*** clautolisp" note on the TYPE function page.
- Tests (autolisp-builtins-core):
  type-symbols-variant-safearray-names-lower-case-except-bricscad
  (autocad-2022, autocad-2026, clautolisp, strict, lax lower case;
  bricscad-v25, bricscad-v26 upper case; the other TYPE results upper
  case everywhere), type-symbols-lower-case-name-is-still-the-same-symbol
  (EQ / READ round trips per dialect, canonical name unchanged).

Side observations, not acted on here:
- (type f) of a DEFUNed function is SUBR on both vendors in this run (the
  probe file may have been loaded compiled); clautolisp's AUTOLISP-TYPE
  returns USUBR for an interpreted DEFUN. Worth a follow-up check.
- AutoCAD's (vlax-get-acad-object) gave nil in this run, so the vla-object
  row has no AutoCAD datum (VLA-OBJECT is upper case as a literal there).
